text.section:
The Apple Board may:

Administer, manage and make expenditures from the Apple Fund;


Plan and conduct campaigns of research, education, publicity, and industry development for the purpose of enhancing the viability and profitability of the Virginia apple industry;


Make contracts to accomplish the purposes of this chapter;


Cooperate with other state, regional, national, and international organizations in research concerning education on promotion of apples, and expend moneys of the Apple Fund for such purposes;


Establish committees of the Apple Board to address horticultural and such other issues as the Apple Board deems pertinent to the Virginia apple industry; and


Do whatever else may be necessary to effectuate the purposes of this chapter.
